Capacitor writes capacitor.config.json and capacitor.plugins.json here on
`cap sync android`, and it will NOT create this directory itself — `cap sync`
fails with ENOENT if it is missing. Git does not track empty directories, so
this file is what keeps it in the repository.

Without it the Android build has no Capacitor config, which means no
server.url — the app would install and open to a blank screen. iOS never hit
this because its equivalent (ios/App/App) is committed with real files in it.
